# Compliance claims honesty (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08): **honesty and integrity are immutable.**
Agents must never claim compliance outcomes the product or lab evidence does
not support. Coding closes *technical* gaps only; it does not certify the
Organization Seeking Assessment (OSA).

## The rule

> **Never claim Met, certified, compliant, assessment-ready, or equivalent
> beyond proven evidence. Prefer Live / Partial / Absent / BLOCKED. Do not
> skip implementation or testing to green-wash a deliverable. Quality and
> completeness are paramount.**

## Toolkit name — not a certification

The live toolkit display name is **`product_name_mark` in
`core-assets/branding/product-identity.json`** (currently **CMMC Complete™**).
Operator chrome interpolates `{{productName}}`. Do not hardcode the SKU
name in locales, honesty banners, or partner copy.

Operator clarification (Phil, 2026-08-22; name file 2026-08-26): the
toolkit name means AIC Server ships the tools an organization needs to
**work toward** CMMC: workforce training and attestation, the
infrastructure they operate, and the tools for secure access.

It does **not** mean the Organization Seeking Assessment is certified, that
a control is Met, or that buying the package finishes an assessment.

| Allowed | Forbidden |
| --- | --- |
| “{toolkit name} is the integrated kit: training, infrastructure, and secure access.” | “{toolkit name} certifies the customer” / “Level *n* in a box = Met” |
| “We provide the tools for Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3.” | “This SKU is CMMC Level 2 certified” |

## Forbidden claims

| Forbidden | Why |
| --- | --- |
| “CMMC certified product” / “CMMC Level 2/3 certified” | CMMC assesses the **OSA**, not a software SKU |
| Using the toolkit name to mean the OSA is certified or a control is Met | The phrase is the toolkit name only — see above |
| **Met** for **PE**, **PS**, facility, visitor escort, personnel screening | Customer / RE — not productizable here |
| **Met** for org **AT** training records / LMS completion | Product is not an LMS |
| **L3 / 800-172 Met** from binder templates or profile toggles | **L3 is not L2 + toggles** |
| **800-53 High Met** from Moderate-oriented enclave alone | High deltas must be proven per control |
| **Unqualified FIPS** while residual `ring` (or other documented gaps) remain | Honesty per [`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc) §4 |
| **Met** from playbook apply, chrome-only Playwright, Admin-Token-only binder, nav crawl, or heading asserts | See sibling proof rules below |
| “IR fully implemented / tested” before Phase 1A–1D acceptance evidence | See IR gap plan honesty gate |
| Soft-pass `smtp_unconfigured` as messaging / IR alert proof | See [`mailpit-messaging-comprehensive-test.mdc`](mailpit-messaging-comprehensive-test.mdc) |

## Required agent behavior

1. **Status vocabulary** — Use **Live**, **Partial**, **Absent**, **BLOCKED**
   for product contribution. Reserve **Met** only when a specific technical
   control is Live **and** the named acceptance proof for that control passed
   in the same change set (and still never for OSA certification).
2. **Proof before done** — When claiming a compliance-relevant feature works,
   name the evidence artifact (Playwright spec + assertion, Mailpit message,
   API status, SHA, screenshot inspected). No artifact → not done.
3. **No skip** — Do not omit acceptance tests listed on the work item / plan
   to finish faster. If blocked (lab down, seat missing), mark **BLOCKED**
   with reason — do not invent PASS.
4. **Binder / CSC honesty** — Refuse or reject Met stamps without
   auditor-usable content / verified rescan. See
   [`assessment-binder-section-content.mdc`](assessment-binder-section-content.mdc).
5. **Plan source** — Coding-closeable sequencing lives in
   `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/cmmc-800-53-closeable-dev-plan.md`. Out-of-scope
   PE/PS/AT/facility rows stay customer forever.
6. **Amend inventories** — When a gap flips status, update
   `cmmc-800-53-full-gap-analysis.md` (or the owning gap doc) in the same
   change set — do not leave stale Partial when Live (or vice versa).

